+/* SDL's joystick layer is thread-affine on macOS: the IOKit/HIDAPI hotplug
+ * callbacks are scheduled on the run loop of the thread that initialised the
+ * subsystem, and only that thread's SDL_GameControllerUpdate delivers them.
+ * Initialising on whichever guest thread called cellPadInit and sweeping from
+ * whichever called cellPadGetData means a controller plugged in after start is
+ * never seen. So the subsystem lives on one dedicated thread, which does all
+ * the SDL work; guest threads only copy its latest snapshot. */
+#define PAD_SDL_SWEEP_MS 2
 
